schema: "0.4"
id: npl-ux-d2-three-pane-triage-chat-thread
type: image
quality: high

# Direction D2: persistent three-pane triage — screen: chat rooms, messages, thread panel with pins & scheduled send
# Nocturne palette (exact hexes, dark-native canvas — never pure #000/#fff): canvas #010409, panel #0d1117, raised #161b22, border #21262d, primary text #e6edf3 (soft off-white ink), secondary text #909dab, muted text #6e7681, signal green (live/primary accent) #3fb950, link cyan (navigation) #58a6ff, amber (rare warning) #d29922, error coral #f85149. Type: Inter for UI/labels, JetBrains Mono (co-equal voice) for counts, timestamps, ids, code, SQL, paths. Shape: flat surfaces separated by lightness steps only, 4px radius, no drop shadows, no glow, no gradients, no neon bloom, no OLED pitch-black, no pure-white surfaces.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity dark-native app UI
    for NoizuPromptLingo. This direction is a PERSISTENT THREE-PANE TRIAGE shell:
    a narrow always-visible nav column (with labels, not icon-only), a middle LIST
    pane, and a right DETAIL pane — an email/ticketing-triage layout optimized for
    fast list traversal (j/k keyboard navigation hinted in the UI). Render as a
    real product screenshot, never a wireframe.
  text: |
        A 16:9 high-fidelity UI mockup of NoizuPromptLingo's Chat screen, testing
        the THREE-PANE TRIAGE shell direction: rooms | messages | thread panel.

        LEFT NAV COLUMN (narrow, ~180px, labeled, persistent): same nav as
        other shots, with "Chat" active (bold + green left edge) expanded
        beneath it into a ROOMS sub-list: "#platform-eng" (selected, unread
        bold), "#agent-ops", "#design-review", "#random" — each with a small
        mono unread count badge except the selected room.

        MIDDLE MESSAGES PANE (panel tone, dominant width): header
        "#platform-eng" with a small "12 members" mono label and a pin icon
        with count "3". Below, a vertical message list: avatar + name + mono
        timestamp, message text bubbles WITHOUT heavy card chrome (flat, just
        hairline-separated), realistic content ("Deploy for sha-302be2c is
        green ✅", "Can someone review NPL-482 before EOD?", "Scheduling the
        retro for Thursday 10am"). One message near the bottom shows a small
        "Scheduled · sends in 2h14m" mono chip instead of a timestamp (a
        composed-but-not-yet-sent scheduled message). A message compose bar at
        the very bottom with a text input, a schedule-send clock icon, and a
        send button.

        RIGHT THREAD PANEL (raised tone #161b22, narrower than messages pane):
        header "Thread" with a small "Pinned" section listing 3 compact pinned-
        message rows (sender + truncated text + mono timestamp), then a
        divider, then the open thread itself — a root message and 2 reply rows
        indented beneath it with connecting hairline, avatars, and mono
        timestamps. A small mute toggle ("🔕 Mute thread") sits near the top
        of the panel, muted styling.

        Use realistic, specific product content throughout — never lorem ipsum.

  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, neon glow, bloom, CRT scanlines, gradient background, pure-black OLED background, pure-white surfaces, warm amber/gold dominant palette, light-mode canvas"

attachments:
  - path: _nocturne-palette.png
    role: reference
    description: "Locked Nocturne palette swatches (bg, surface, border, text, muted, accent, success, danger) with hex labels — match these exact colors, do not reinterpret."

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

service: gemini
provider_options:
  generate_content_model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Shows persistent labeled nav with Chat expanded to a rooms list, a middle message stream with a scheduled-send chip and compose bar, and a right thread panel showing pinned messages, a threaded reply chain, and a mute toggle"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Dark-native Nocturne canvas (#010409/#0d1117), single phosphor-green #3fb950 signal, link cyan #58a6ff, amber #d29922 used sparingly, mono-first counts/timestamps/ids in JetBrains Mono, 4px radius, flat surface-step elevation, no shadow/glow/gradient"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Three clear vertical panes, rooms list narrow, messages pane dominant, thread panel distinctly a supporting rail on the right"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "neon glow, bloom, or gradient wash"
    - "light-mode or warm/gold dominant canvas instead of dark-native Nocturne"

tags: [ux-overhaul, npl-nocturne, NoizuPromptLingo, shell-direction, direction-2]
